      "location": "Example",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "For n>1, the vertical maps are ×n, ×n, and 0. Hence ker(×n)=0, ker(0)=Z/n, and both coker(×n) and coker(0) are Z/n. The snake sequence must therefore contain coker(×n)=Z/n and coker(0)=Z/n after the displayed connecting-map target. The page instead asserts 0 → 0 → 0 → Z/n →δ Z/n → 0 → 0. Taking n=2 gives two omitted nonzero terms, so the asserted sequence is false.",
