      "evidence": "Step 1.1 says to “replace Y by the image of γ and Y' by the image of the same composite in the bottom row,” then asserts that the rows induce a morphism of short exact sequences and that the snake lemma gives coker(β) ↪ coker(γ). No replacement maps, short exact rows, or morphism of short exact sequences are specified. The cited thm-snake-lemma-in-an-abelian-category applies only to its displayed Mac Lane morphism of short exact sequences, so it does not license this asserted injection.",
